src/services/purchaseRequisitionService.ts: createPR() and submitPR() enforce company/branch ownership, FY/period, Expected Delivery Date policy, PR Type eligibility, and duplicate PRs, but perform no validation of Global Item approval, Branch Item Availability activation, Branch Category consistency, effective UOM/conversion, MOQ, or Order Multiple.
12. Existing RFQ / PO / Inventory Dependencies
RFQ (src/services/rfqService.ts & prRfqConversionService.ts): Reads UOM conversions via uomConversionService.getUomSnapshot(itemCode) and stores transaction-level purchaseUom, inventoryUom, conversionRatio, and category snapshots on RfqLineItem.
PO (src/services/purchaseOrderService.ts): Consumes uomConversionService and preserves purchaseUom, inventoryUom, conversionRatio, itemCategory snapshots on PurchaseOrderLine.
GRN (src/services/goodsReceiptService.ts): Converts receivedQtyPurchUom -> convertedQtyInvUom via l.conversionRatio || uomSnap.conversionRatio, posts accepted stock to inventoryValidationService, and enforces FY posting gates.
Inventory Validation & Aging (inventoryValidationService.ts, inventoryAgingService.ts): Stock balances (InventoryBalanceRecord) and batch/lot expiry (InventoryBatchLotRecord) store itemCode, warehouseCode, branchId, uom, itemCategory, batchNo, expiryDate, reusing Branch.warehouses. They do not yet read Branch Item Availability flags (batchTracking, lotTracking, shelfLifeControlled, serialTracking, qualityInspection, preferred/eligible warehouses).
