Existing seed/runtime records (INITIAL_GLOBAL_ITEMS, INITIAL_BRANCH_ITEM_CLASSIFICATIONS, INITIAL_PRS, INITIAL_RFQS, INITIAL_POS, INITIAL_GOODS_RECEIPTS, INITIAL_INVENTORY_BALANCES) use global items with categoryCode (RM, FG, MA), legacy codes (RMPAOPOEXLG0001, FGHDMCRGY0002, MAPALBL0003), and compliance fields directly on GlobalItem.
Migration Requirements & Impact:
Preserve all existing Global Item IDs, Global Item Codes, Descriptions, and historical PR/RFQ/PO/GRN/Inventory transaction snapshots without recalculation.
Extract categoryCode + compliance (shelfLifeControl, serialNumberControl, warrantyPolicy, moq, orderMultiple, branchAvailability) from each legacy GlobalItem into Branch Item Availability records where (Company, Branch) ownership is unambiguous (e.g., INITIAL_BRANCH_ITEM_CLASSIFICATIONS), and flag ambiguous/unmapped records as MIGRATION_REVIEW_REQUIRED (inactive until verified) without guessing.
